Notebook[{Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Riemannian Infrageometry", "GuideTitle", 
      CellID -> 942062912, ExpressionUUID -> 
       "a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"], 
     Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Reviewed by Pavel Hajek on 18 October 2026.", 
        "TI"]], "GuideAbstract", CellID -> 2001916300, 
      ExpressionUUID -> "ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"], 
     Cell[TextData[
       {"Riemannian Infrageometry describes and distinguishes graphs as ", 
        StyleBox["geometric substrates", FontWeight -> "Bold"], ". In \
contrast, synthetic infrageometry asks only whether certain postulates are \
satisfied by the substrate so that its propositions about geometric objects \
hold."}], "GuideAbstract", CellID -> 2001916300, ExpressionUUID -> 
       "ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"], 
     Cell[TextData[{"Riemann viewed space as an infinitesimal webbing of \
paths and, by imposing conditions on the infinitesimal length element, \
arrived at the ", StyleBox["quadratic metric tensor", FontWeight -> "Bold"], 
        " as the lowest-order data satisfying those conditions. This split \
continuous geometry into a manifold, which carries the topology and global \
analysis, and a Riemannian structure. This led people such as Gromov to ask \
about the moduli space of Riemannian structures on a fixed manifold, or, \
conversely, to derive topological quantities from Riemannian ones."}], 
      "GuideAbstract", CellID -> 2001916300, ExpressionUUID -> 
       "ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"], 
     Cell[TextData[{"In infrageometry, the discrete webbing of paths given by \
a graph is itself the geometric substrate, so no such split occurs. We relate \
infrageometry to continuous geometry through ", 
        StyleBox["rescaled Gromov\[Dash]Hausdorff convergence", 
         FontWeight -> "Bold"], ", where the scaling is determined by the \
observer's scale. This yields a generalized definition of geometry: if a \
limit of rescaled graphs is a metric space arising from a Riemannian \
manifold, then that manifold is uniquely determined up to isomorphism."}], 
      "GuideAbstract", CellID -> 2001916300, ExpressionUUID -> 
       "ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"], 
     Cell[TextData[{"A geodesic at observer scale ", 
        Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "d298c7bb-7b58-48bb-8110-3b4cc90423c6"], " of length ", 
        Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "e0ae8f67-ef13-4d3f-bcea-4296331b881d"], ", ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData["InfraGeodesic"]], 
              "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraGeodesic", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{StyleBox["germ", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["r", "TI"], 
              ",", " ", StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "ae89a744-b584-456b-9313-c56e74a2ba1c"], 
        ", is a family of walks of length ", 
        Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "c4588c28-5313-4a6a-9c39-e01d5888b42c"], 
        " that are shortest paths in every window of ", 
        Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "01149153-8348-4c7e-9d03-bc3225174749"], 
        " edges. A representative can be found with ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                "RandomInfraGeodesic"]], "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeomet\
ry/ref/RandomInfraGeodesic", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            "\[Ellipsis]", "]"}]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 
          0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "e1f4e417-9540-416f-8335-c3c8770a5b6a"], 
        ", and the edge density of the corresponding multi-object with ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
              "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["geodesic", 
               "TI"], ",", " ", "\"EdgeDensity\""}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "d5db17a3-7c0e-4dff-84b6-0e622e4abf8c"], "."}], "GuideAbstract", 
      CellID -> 2001916300, ExpressionUUID -> 
       "ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"], 
     Cell[TextData[{"We can measure the volumes of ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData["InfraBall"]], 
              "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraBall", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["r0", "TI"]}], 
            "]"}]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, 
         ExpressionUUID -> "7fce9d4e-d699-4d13-acf0-3758e491b471"], " for ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{SubscriptBox[StyleBox["r", "TI"], "0"], 
            "\[LessEqual]", StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "b53fca9b-a722-456c-8d89-4f5a9383e4f0"], ", ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData["InfraTube"]], 
              "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraTube", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{StyleBox["axis", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
            "]"}]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, 
         ExpressionUUID -> "4c90ec4f-f4e5-466b-b7e9-9d84908ae193"], 
        " for any ray or line through ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
         "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "27adf971-ca16-44ac-8409-968fb97dd1da"], " and any thickness ", 
        Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "9eee7ac8-e28d-4942-b99d-386c26acee9b"], ", and ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData["InfraCone"]], 
              "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraCone", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{StyleBox["axis", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], 
            "]"}]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, 
         ExpressionUUID -> "866940c5-cfe8-4aff-94d5-0e7697d7d9c8"], 
        " for slope ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "e9e4245b-2cff-48e7-b4fd-dc68adac8f96"], ". Such measurements have \
asymptotic expansions in the continuous case and can be used to determine ", 
        StyleBox["limiting curvature components", FontWeight -> "Bold"], 
        ". However, no sphere structure exists a priori on ", 
        Cell[BoxData[TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData["InfraShell"]], 
            "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraShell", 
            "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, "PackageLink", 
           BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "48e208b6-fc37-4858-864d-7ca379ba4159"], ", so the \
limiting linear tensors can be compared only through histograms. We can also \
obtain the histogram of mutual distances between points, which constrains the \
limiting Riemannian manifold."}], "GuideAbstract", CellID -> 2001916300, 
      ExpressionUUID -> "ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"], 
     Cell[TextData[{"We have ", Cell[BoxData[
          RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData["InfraTangentBundle"]], 
              "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraTangentBundle", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], 
            "]"}]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, 
         ExpressionUUID -> "b439bef0-e1bc-46dc-920b-9336bf193d25"], 
        " which represents vectors at p by rays of length ", 
        Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "272bedd6-d906-4a8d-9e21-851285c6ec09"], ", and these are compactly \
encoded as chains in the spray graph at ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
         "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "794bb1d6-a638-4f48-8863-91988e14b249"], 
        ". We have an even simpler infra-bundle, ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                "InfraDisplacementBundle"]], "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGe\
ometry/ref/InfraDisplacementBundle", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], 
            "]"}]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, 
         ExpressionUUID -> "7f976ca5-621e-4480-a9c3-f609a5904890"], ", that \
keeps only the endpoints of rays. We have a minimal model of the Levi-Civita \
connection, ", Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                "FindInfraLeviCivitaConnection"]], "paclet:WolframInstitute/I\
nfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraLeviCivitaConnection", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[", RowBox[{StyleBox["g", 
                 "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}], "]"}]], 
         "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "ad3ee6e6-352f-45dd-8804-fbab864042d6"], ", and ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                "InfraParallelTransport"]], "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeo\
metry/ref/InfraParallelTransport", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[", RowBox[
                 {StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], 
                "]"}], ",", " ", StyleBox["walk", "TI"]}], "]"}]], 
         "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "d25ddd83-9ae4-4804-863f-e8d271bb5339"], "."}], "GuideAbstract", 
      CellID -> 2001916300, ExpressionUUID -> 
       "ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"], 
     Cell[TextData[{"We also have ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                "InfraMetricTensor"]], 
              "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMetricTensor", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", 
              " ", StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "acbfca66-2760-462c-9f7c-93bb244b5adb"], ", which computes shortest \
path projections of rays, displacement commutator ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                "DisplacementCommutator"]], "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeo\
metry/ref/DisplacementCommutator", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["d1", "TI"], ",", 
              " ", StyleBox["d2", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "31be6d84-4f82-4ff4-a951-d77d5e70bdeb"], 
        ", and addition of displacements via midpoints with ", 
        Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData["DisplacementSum"]], 
              "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/DisplacementSum", 
              "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
             "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"], "[", 
            RowBox[{StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", StyleBox["d1", "TI"], ",", 
              " ", StyleBox["d2", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula", 
         FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
          "da646df7-15c2-4a39-ad6a-5a25d6e7ae5a"], 
        ". These can be used to illustrate ", 
        StyleBox["emergence of linearity", FontWeight -> "Bold"], "."}], 
      "GuideAbstract", CellID -> 2001916300, ExpressionUUID -> 
       "ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]}, Open]], 
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["", "GuideFunctionsSection", CellID -> 1866139230, 
      ExpressionUUID -> "a0ea3657-4c83-4862-93c8-ecf80cebc774"], 
     Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Infrageodesics", "GuideFunctionsSubsection", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "1b2b90ce-13fe-4ef5-b1df-bca408528547"], 
        Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                 "InfraGeodesic"]], 
               "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraGeodesic", 
               "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
              "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"]], 
            "InlineGuideFunction", TaggingRules -> 
             {"PageType" -> "Function"}, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "6efc5ab4-ba95-4ed2-a3fb-691d76eb4024"], " \[LongDash] ", 
           "the geodesics at infra-scale ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["s", 
              "TI"]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, 
            ExpressionUUID -> "eb82456e-9d54-4f40-ab8a-168feaa51384"], " \
through a germ, walks that are shortest paths in every window of ", 
           Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
            FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "fd1c0a5e-f060-47d5-acb5-a3f11f28e446"], " steps"}], 
         "GuideText", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "ae4b5e81-a1ee-4d3b-bf83-c3272155f0bc"], 
        Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                 "RandomInfraGeodesic"]], "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeome\
try/ref/RandomInfraGeodesic", 
               "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
              "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"]], 
            "InlineGuideFunction", TaggingRules -> 
             {"PageType" -> "Function"}, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "da67e090-73fd-46ed-8975-4b1dc448ef87"], " \[LongDash] ", 
           "random geodesics at infra-scale ", 
           Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
            FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "a01851df-a3a6-4d29-bdd8-5fd19bb33ab2"], 
           " grown from a vertex or a walk"}], "GuideText", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "0027775c-8481-4d72-b791-738d201c5251"], 
        Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                 "InfraGeodesicQ"]], 
               "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraGeodesicQ", 
               "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
              "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"]], 
            "InlineGuideFunction", TaggingRules -> 
             {"PageType" -> "Function"}, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "e5ff79c5-5e77-43d2-af73-203817217ba0"], " \[LongDash] ", 
           "whether a walk is a geodesic at infra-scale ", 
           Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
            FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "07385144-2312-4049-8461-36c0265eaa47"]}], "GuideText", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "77f5fc2f-d00c-4438-b6d8-7e8bfbe651e9"], 
        Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[StyleBox[
                  "FindShortestPath", FontSlant -> "Italic"]]], 
               "paclet:ref/FindShortestPath"}, "RefLink", BaseStyle -> 
               "InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction", TaggingRules -> 
             {"PageType" -> "Function"}, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "c727da73-305f-4f07-b15e-6c1a6ff40384"], " (WL)", 
           " \[LongDash] ", 
           "a geodesic at infinite scale, a shortest path"}], "GuideText", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "de240ab6-e062-4900-bd5b-8cc51cb0e283"], 
        Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                 "InfraWalkQ"]], 
               "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraWalkQ", 
               "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
              "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"]], 
            "InlineGuideFunction", TaggingRules -> 
             {"PageType" -> "Function"}, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "e868f62c-d1df-4207-a382-f4142929280c"], ", ", 
           Cell[BoxData[TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData["InfraSegmentQ"]], 
               "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSegmentQ", 
               "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
              "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"]], 
            "InlineGuideFunction", TaggingRules -> 
             {"PageType" -> "Function"}, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "2386fd63-bd79-4913-a6c2-661476d38263"]}], "GuideText", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "8f22cb12-57fb-4534-bc36-701fd4ab26ab"]}, Open]], 
     Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Straight walks", "GuideFunctionsSubsection", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "e4ebfa50-afd3-40d5-9af0-5241221a3b15"], 
        Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[TemplateBox[{Cell[TextData[
                 "RandomInfraWalk"]], 
               "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraWalk", 
               "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"}, 
              "PackageLink", BaseStyle -> "InlineFormula"]], 
            "InlineGuideFunction", TaggingRules -> 
             {"PageType" -> "Function"}, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "643b59e0-9fc0-4a25-b3eb-1907fcd0a66e"], " \[LongDash] ", 
           "walks grown from a germ; ", Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[
                {"\"Geodesic\"", ",", " ", RowBox[{"\"Straightness\"", " ", 
                   "->", " ", "\[Beta]"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula", 
            FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "73136416-37c3-49ac-b05f-ed6ec028516a"], 
           " weighs each step by its mean gain, and the bare ", 
           Cell[BoxData["\"Geodesic\""], "InlineFormula", 
            FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "3966e1b6-cebc-48a2-95c0-fe2f8bb58e65"], 
           " is a shortest path"}], "GuideText", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "d8834e4f-376f-46b8-8b6b-7cb03a62400b"], 
        Cell[TextData[{"A step from the tip ", 
           Cell[BoxData[SubscriptBox[StyleBox["w", "TI"], StyleBox["t", 
               "TI"]]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, 
            ExpressionUUID -> "3cf624db-7c85-41b5-8834-f553cf8af20f"], 
           " of the window ", Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{StyleBox["(", 
                SpanMaxSize -> 1], RowBox[{SubscriptBox[StyleBox["w", "TI"], 
                  "0"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", SubscriptBox[StyleBox["w", 
                   "TI"], StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], StyleBox[")", 
                SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 
             0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "4464c0cd-7b78-4aae-b831-38e2bedb0389"], " to a neighbour ", 
           Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["v", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", 
            FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "8947a14d-0727-4e68-b787-148d77a3a076"], " has the gain ", 
           Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{SubscriptBox[StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
                  StyleBox["i", "TI"]], StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
                 StyleBox["v", "TI"], StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1], "=", 
                 StyleBox["d", "TI"], StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
                 RowBox[{SubscriptBox[StyleBox["w", "TI"], StyleBox["i", 
                     "TI"]], ",", StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], StyleBox[")", 
                  SpanMaxSize -> 1], "-", StyleBox["d", "TI"], StyleBox["(", 
                  SpanMaxSize -> 1], RowBox[{SubscriptBox[StyleBox["w", 
                     "TI"], StyleBox["i", "TI"]], ",", SubscriptBox[
                    StyleBox["w", "TI"], StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], 
                 StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1], "\[Element]", "{", "-", 
                 "1"}], ",", "0", ",", RowBox[{"1", "}"}]}]], 
            "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "1354505a-889b-48a8-9f5c-788f7d313849"], 
           " against each earlier vertex, and the mean gain ", 
           Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{StyleBox["g", "TI"], StyleBox["(", 
                SpanMaxSize -> 1], StyleBox["v", "TI"], StyleBox[")", 
                SpanMaxSize -> 1], "=", FractionBox["1", StyleBox["t", 
                 "TI"]], UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", RowBox[{StyleBox["i", 
                   "TI"], "<", StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], LimitsPositioning -> 
                 False], SubscriptBox[StyleBox["g", "TI"], StyleBox["i", 
                 "TI"]], StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], StyleBox["v", 
                "TI"], StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]], "InlineFormula", 
            FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "84041c03-26f4-46e5-93f7-e09bca604ca0"], "."}], "GuideText", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "990f003b-053b-4810-9237-d4f121598660"], 
        Cell[TextData[{"The walk draws ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["v", "TI"]], 
            "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "0dd106c9-0c10-457e-ab9a-226beb9f9a08"], 
           " with probability proportional to ", 
           Cell[BoxData[SuperscriptBox[StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
              RowBox[{StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
                StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
                StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]]], "InlineFormula", 
            FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "a1c71a36-ee8f-4e60-9b92-6665f506556d"], ". Only differences of \
scores matter, so the mean gain ranks like the total distance ", 
           Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", RowBox[
                 {StyleBox["i", "TI"], "<", StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
                LimitsPositioning -> False], StyleBox["d", "TI"], StyleBox[
                "(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], RowBox[{SubscriptBox[StyleBox["w", 
                   "TI"], StyleBox["i", "TI"]], ",", StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], 
               StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]], "InlineFormula", 
            FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, ExpressionUUID -> 
             "edc95079-cc1f-4c2d-bea7-30a190d1290b"], 
           " to the window, and the exponential is the only such weight."}], 
         "GuideText", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "c24bed50-36f5-43e3-99f1-798413b6da16"], 
        Cell[TextData[{"On a mesh whose path distance is a rounding of the \
Euclidean distance, ", Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{StyleBox["g", "TI"], StyleBox[
                "(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], StyleBox["v", "TI"], StyleBox[")", 
                SpanMaxSize -> 1], "\[TildeTilde]", StyleBox["cos", 
                FontSlant -> "Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", StyleBox["\[Theta]", 
                "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, 
            ExpressionUUID -> "8d11bee4-7b56-43bf-83fa-eb2f7767ccb5"], 
           " for a turn by the angle ", Cell[BoxData[StyleBox["\[Theta]", 
              "TI"]], "InlineFormula", FontSize -> 0.9*Inherited, 
            ExpressionUUID -> "787871be-f431-4495-8309-961ee6f4ff48"], ", \
since the roundings up and down balance along a window not aligned with the \
