direction vertices, preserving each germ's geodesic-interval excess during \
extension"}], "GuideText"], Cell[TextData[
          {"", StyleBox["RectilinearCoordinates", "InlineCode"], " maps every \
vertex to signed integer nearest-axis coordinates from a frame ", 
           StyleBox["{O, A, B, C}", "InlineCode"], 
           ", or any number of directions"}], "GuideText"], 
        Cell[TextData[{"The spatial graph must be connected, simple, \
undirected, unweighted and untagged. The default ", 
           StyleBox["\"SelectCoordinate\" -> Min", "InlineCode"], 
           " chooses the smallest signed position at a projection tie; ", 
           StyleBox["Max", "InlineCode"], ", ", StyleBox["First", 
            "InlineCode"], " and ", StyleBox["Last", "InlineCode"], 
           " are also supported. The ", StyleBox["\"Axes\"", "InlineCode"], " \
option accepts explicit oriented geodesic vertex lists. The axes need not be \
orthogonal, and different vertices can receive the same coordinate tuple. Use \
this association as the projection of ", StyleBox["InfraFiberedGraph", 
            "InlineCode"], " to retain the corresponding fibers. "}], 
         "GuideText"]}, Open]]}, Open]], 
